## Code Review

### Correctness
❌ `import_step_1.php` displays the third-level leaf select before the middle master-setting group select, so the Step 1 layout becomes `人事設定` -> leaf -> group instead of `人事設定` -> group -> leaf as required by the reference images.

### Security
✅ No new SQL, file upload parsing, auth, or user-controlled HTML rendering was introduced in the reviewed diff. The new JS uses role-filtered `menu_selection.setting_hr.detail` before showing leaf options.

### Test Coverage
⚠️ No browser/manual QA was run because repo instructions prohibit Browser/manual QA on Jinji. Static checks cover syntax, group order, backend schema intersection, and selected UI invariants; the failed DOM-order check needs a code fix.

### Code Quality
⚠️ The grouped map is clear and ordered, but the existing middle-select DOM placement was reused without adapting the order for a 3-level `setting_hr` UI. `所属` option leaves also need the same Step 1 change-state handling as other setting_hr leaves.

### Detailed Findings

#### Critical Issues (must fix)
- `application/modules/common/views/import/import_step_1.php:33` and `application/modules/common/views/import/import_step_1.php:39` — `.menu_details` is rendered before `#js-midItems`. CSS renders `.format_item__content` children in DOM order, so the UI order cannot match `image_1101648705_0/1/2` where the group select is second and the leaf select is third.
- `application/modules/common/assets/hr/js/import/import_index.js:517` — the `menu_details` change handler has no branch for `isAffiliationOptionMasterSetting(menu_detail)`. After choosing `所属 > 任意項目1/2/3`, template filtering/state can remain from the previous leaf even though those leaves have separate `項目名称` fields.

#### Warnings (should fix)
- `application/modules/common/views/import/import_step_1.php:39` — the PHP fallback options inside `#js-selectMidItems` still render only employee details. JS repopulates the select for `setting_hr`, but the server-rendered fallback is inconsistent if JS initialization fails or is delayed.

#### Suggestions (nice to have)
- Add a small static/unit-like check for import Step 1 select order and grouped `setting_hr` map consistency, because this screen has both tracked template assets and active nested common assets.

